# Global → Local position correction request (internal nav frame, metres).
# Identity fields are mandatory; identity-less legacy requests are rejected.
#
# session_id / epoch_id — Local SLAM reference that originated the computation.
# keyframe_id           — keyframe that triggered the originating GS step.
# correction_id         — unique id for this correction emission (idempotency).
#                         Scope: Global SLAM instance (high bits = boot nonce).
# type                  — "bundle_adjustment" | "close_loop"
#                         (apply-gate family; loops share close_loop gates)
# source                — G6d origin: "ba" | "tag_loop" | "visual_loop"
#                         Empty treated as inferred from type for compatibility.
#
# Response (G5):
#   accepted — admitted for processing (not merely "looks valid").
#   applied  — EKF state was mutated by at least one axis.
#   applied_delta_* — actual translation applied in internal nav (after gates).
#   outcome:
#     rejected | applied | gated_noop | busy | localslam_disabled |
#     not_initialized | reset_before_apply | apply_timeout
# Do not treat accepted=true alone as application success.

float64 delta_x
float64 delta_y
float64 delta_z
string type
string source
unique_identifier_msgs/UUID session_id
uint64 epoch_id
uint64 keyframe_id
uint64 correction_id
---
bool accepted
string reason
bool applied
float64 applied_delta_x
float64 applied_delta_y
float64 applied_delta_z
string outcome
